From c4a51ad971dda022261fbd3599e86403a322e6a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:47:06 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 065/152] PCI: dwc: Add Samsung Exynos9810 PCIe Gen2 driver

Add a root complex driver for PCIe channel 0 of Exynos9810, which
connects the Broadcom Wi-Fi chip on Galaxy S9 / Tab Active3 class
devices. The sequences follow Samsung's GPL kernel (pci-exynos.c,
pci-exynos9810_cal.c): PMU PHY isolation release, PHY power-down clear,
sysreg lane setup, PCS/MAC/PHY reset pulses through ELBI, the 26 MHz Gen2
PMA tables, CDR reset, then LTSSM enable with up to ten retries.

While the link is down every DBI access is bracketed with the PCS
"ignore RX electrical idle" bit and NCLK control, as the vendor driver
does, since the core clock is otherwise gated and the access hangs.
INTx is delivered on the controller's own GIC line; MSI and ASPM are not
used (the L1.2 CDR-reset sequencer is not programmed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Kconfig           |  13 +
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Makefile          |   1 +
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-exynos9810.c | 679 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 693 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-exynos9810.c

